      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__i3cpsx__api_1gabd02b8629475df4910710b6f3ab6c73b" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void XI3cPsx_RecoverFromError</definition>
        <argsstring>(XI3cPsx *InstancePtr)</argsstring>
        <name>XI3cPsx_RecoverFromError</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_i3c_psx" kindref="compound">XI3cPsx</ref> *</type>
          <declname>InstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Brings the controller back to a usable state after a transfer error. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>An error response such as a receive buffer overflow leaves the core halted, and it stays halted until RESUME is written. The FIFOs are cleared after that because a transfer aborted part way through can leave untransmitted data behind in the TX FIFO.</para><para>This does not restore a target that has latched an error into its CCC_DEVICE_STATUS; that register is read only and needs the controller to read it with GETSTATUS.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_i3c_psx" kindref="compound">XI3cPsx</ref> instance.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>RESUME must be written before the FIFOs are reset. Resetting the FIFOs of a halted core leaves it halted. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
